  "requirements_dev": "# Development-only Python environment for the repository's scripts: tests, analysis\n# and plotting tools, asset and artwork pipelines, build helpers and the music\n# pipeline core. Nothing here ships with or is loaded by the game, the relay or the\n# online platform; see \"Dependencies\" in AGENTS.md for the dev/runtime split.\n#\n#   uv venv --python 3.11 .venv\n#   uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements-dev.txt\n#\n# Included sets keep their own pins and remain the source of truth for them:\n-r tools/asset-requirements.txt\n-r tools/music/requirements.txt\n-r tools/docs/requirements.txt\n#\n# Kept out on purpose:\n# - mobile/play-api-requirements.txt: hash-pinned, isolated venv for Play uploads.\n# - tools/music/requirements-{synth,samples,separation,genai}.txt: large or\n#   hardware-specific extras (pedalboard, torch/Demucs, ACE-Step).\n# - bpy, bmesh, mathutils (Blender), gimpfu (GIMP) and gi (PyGObject) come from the\n#   host application or system packages, not pip.\n\n# Data analysis and plotting. numpy and scipy repeat the music pipeline's pins;\n# change both files together.\nnumpy==2.4.6\nscipy==1.17.1\nscikit-learn==1.9.1\npandas==3.0.6\nmatplotlib==3.11.2\n\n# Build, web asset and deployment helpers\nscons==4.11.1\nfonttools==4.66.1\nbrotli==1.2.0\nPyYAML==6.0.3\n\n# Map toolkit binding generation; pair with the system libclang 18 library.\nclang==18.1.8\n"
